Phoenix-RTOS: make SDL's pthread detection (CheckPTHREAD) succeed.

libphoenix integrates pthreads into the libc, so there is no separate
-lpthread to link, and the aarch64-phoenix gcc rejects the "-pthread" driver
flag (it is not a recognized option). SDL's default detection tries one of
those and the link/compile test fails, so HAVE_SDL_THREADS is never set and
the build stops at "Threads ... may not be disabled". Adding a PHOENIX case
that uses no extra pthread flags lets the pthread_attr_init() probe pass.

Upstreamable as-is (guarded by the PHOENIX cmake variable this port sets).

--- a/cmake/sdlchecks.cmake	2024-07-29 16:22:29.000000000 +0200
+++ b/cmake/sdlchecks.cmake	2026-08-04 22:44:56.587048110 +0200
@@ -938,7 +938,11 @@
 # PTHREAD_LIBS
 macro(CheckPTHREAD)
   if(SDL_THREADS AND SDL_PTHREADS)
-    if(ANDROID)
+    if(PHOENIX)
+      # Phoenix-RTOS: pthreads are integrated into libphoenix (the libc); there
+      # is no separate -lpthread to link and gcc rejects the -pthread driver
+      # flag. No extra compile/link flags are needed.
+    elseif(ANDROID)
       # the android libc provides built-in support for pthreads, so no
       # additional linking or compile flags are necessary
     elseif(LINUX)
